  "query_preview": "..\n\nExtremely little changes to the overall long term forecast, with\nthe only large scale feature of note being a surge of energy from\nthe eastern Bering Sea possibly moving into the northern Alaska\nGulf by this weekend. Details are still low on this possible\nevent, but worse case scenario from current solutions is another\nround of moderate to possibly heavy rain for primarily the\nnorthern half of the panhandle, along with an increase in winds.\nOtherwise, mid to late work week has multiple waves move through\nmainly the northern half of the panhandle. These waves do not look\nto bring rain totals greater than an inch, with rain rates not\nexceeding light intensity.",
